<%#
  EXECUTIVE BRIEFING

  Route:   GET  /assessment/instructions
           POST /assessment/start   → creates the attempt, stamps started_at and
                                      deadline_at (+10 min), assigns the 20
                                      randomised permutations, redirects to
                                      /assessment/questions/1
  Layout:  nav: 'default'

  Locals
    title        String
    csrfToken    String
    participant  Object   { full_name, participant_number }
    resuming     Boolean? true when an IN_PROGRESS attempt already exists.
                          The submit button becomes "Resume assessment" and
                          POST /assessment/start must NOT reset the deadline.

  This is the last screen before the clock starts. It says so plainly rather
  than burying it.
%>

<div class="container container-narrow section">

  <div class="label-meta">Step 2 of 3 &middot; Briefing</div>
  <h1 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,34px)">Before you begin</h1>
  <p class="text-muted" style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:var(--sp-5)">
    Read this carefully. Once you start, the timer runs continuously and cannot
    be paused.
  </p>

  <div class="metric-grid" style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-5)">
    <div class="metric">
      <span class="metric-value">20</span>
      <div class="metric-label">Questions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <span class="metric-value">10</span>
      <div class="metric-label">Minutes</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <span class="metric-value">20</span>
      <div class="metric-label">Total marks</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <span class="metric-value">01</span>
      <div class="metric-label">Attempt</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-lg">
    <h3>Structure</h3>
    <div class="row" style="gap:var(--sp-3);align-items:stretch;margin-bottom:var(--sp-5)">
      <div class="card card-sunk" style="flex:1;min-width:200px;padding:var(--sp-4)">
        <span class="badge badge-accent">SECTION A</span>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size:14px;margin:var(--sp-3) 0 0">
          Questions 1&ndash;10 &middot; 10 marks
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-sunk" style="flex:1;min-width:200px;padding:var(--sp-4)">
        <span class="badge badge-accent">SECTION B</span>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size:14px;margin:var(--sp-3) 0 0">
          Questions 11&ndash;20 &middot; 10 marks
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>How it works</h3>
    <ul class="text-muted" style="font-size:15px;padding-left:var(--sp-5);margin:0 0 var(--sp-5)">
      <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">Each question has four options. Select one.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">Answers save automatically as you select them. There is no save button.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">You may move backwards and forwards, and change any answer until you submit.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">Option order is randomised per officer, so your option B is not your neighbour's option B.</li>
      <li>Unanswered questions score zero. There is no penalty for a wrong answer, so answer everything.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>When time runs out</h3>
    <p class="text-muted" style="font-size:15px;margin-bottom:var(--sp-5)">
      At ten minutes the assessment submits itself automatically with whatever
      you have answered so far. The timer turns amber at two minutes remaining.
    </p>

    <%#
      Disclosure, stated plainly and before they begin.

      Monitoring people without telling them is not something to do quietly,
      and it is also less effective: a rule nobody knows about cannot deter, it
      can only catch. Saying it here is what turns this from surveillance into
      a condition of the assessment.
    %>
    <h3>Keep this window open</h3>
    <p class="text-muted" style="font-size:15px;margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">
      The assessment must remain open in a single window until you submit. If
      you switch tabs, minimise the window, or leave the page, this is recorded
      and the facilitator is notified.
    </p>
    <ul class="text-muted" style="font-size:15px;padding-left:var(--sp-5);margin:0">
      <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">The first occurrence is a warning shown on screen.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-2)">After that your session ends and your PIN stops working.
        You would need a new PIN from the facilitator to continue.</li>
      <li>Your answers are always saved, and the ten-minute limit keeps running.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="alert" style="margin-top:var(--sp-4)">
    This is a baseline diagnostic, not a pass or fail examination. It measures
    where the cohort is starting from so the training can be pitched correctly.
    Correct answers are never shown to participants.
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/assessment/start" style="margin-top:var(--sp-5)">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' ? csrfToken : '' %>">
    <div class="row" style="gap:var(--sp-3)">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-terracotta btn-lg">
        <span><%= typeof resuming !== 'undefined' && resuming ? 'Resume assessment' : 'Start the ten minutes' %></span>
        <svg class="btn-arrow" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20"
             fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M7 4l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
      <a href="/assessment/confirm" class="btn btn-ghost">Back</a>
    </div>
  </form>

</div>
